# Classified safe-cost BOM skeleton

## Scope and acceptance boundary

T-E3-030 classifies cost obligations and records a reusable skeleton. It supplies no prices, usage quantities, monetary totals, budget ceilings, numeric scale triggers, invoices, metering or purchases. Financial readiness, live safe-stop/drain implementation and physical activation remain HELD; T-E3-001-R1 remains REVIEW. Classification describes the assurance required for an enabled capability, not a paid service selection.

Use the scenario sheets and evidence/authorization fields in `[[vault/PROFILES/platform-bom-inputs.md]]` for minimum-safe closed test, minimum-safe Android production, later scale bands, incident month, restore drill and exit drill. Compare candidates on identical capability, workload, custody, assurance and support scope. Recurring, one-off, incident and drill costs stay separate; allocations prevent omissions and double counting. Unknown cost is not zero. Free allowances never replace mandatory assurance.

## Classification rules

- **mandatory:** required for the chosen enabled capability's authority, safety, custody, recovery or operation. A missing price or exhausted budget cannot downgrade this class.
- **deferrable:** capability is explicitly disabled/HELD and its pending work, data, custody and recovery duties remain covered. Record the owner-readable unavailable outcome and exact dependent tasks. Deferral does not make its safeguards optional when enabled.
- **optional:** demonstrably additive convenience with no authority, safety, recovery, required accessibility or support dependence. Require an evidence-backed omission case before purchase or exclusion; no current safeguard qualifies by mere label.
- **scale-triggered:** extra capacity above a proven minimum-safe baseline. Trigger, measurement and threshold are HELD until separately evidenced/authorized; baseline assurance stays mandatory.

Every row below inherits scenario, capability/environment/generation, charge unit/type, workload source/date, current official price validity, tax/currency/FX treatment, allowance/overage/expiry, account/custody/egress dependencies, technical actor, shared allocation, uncertainty, independent verdict and owner budget authorization slots from T-E3-015. All financial slots remain UNFILLED/HELD. Each later row needs exact references, a classification rationale and closure evidence. No implementation product, provider, region, plan or runtime is selected.

## Cost-family classification skeleton

| Family | Baseline class and reason | Bounded deferral / optional / scale treatment | Current readiness |
|---|---|---|---|
| API compute and canonical DB | mandatory for enabled command/status/read authority, current tuple, transactions and retained state | additional capacity scale-triggered; long-work feature may be deferrable, never moved into synchronous callbacks | HELD |
| Durable queue and workers | mandatory for enabled long-effect work: stable operation/effect keys, leases, reconciliation, bounded retry and retained backlog | all dependent long-job capabilities can be deferrable only while disabled and retained work safely handled; extra throughput scale-triggered | HELD |
| Protected audit and independent fallback/custody | mandatory before affected positive effects, including degraded/incident operation | no safety deferral; excess convenience analytics optional only after proven separation | HELD |
| Current negative floors and epoch propagation | mandatory across every enabled runtime, object, cache, worker and recovery edge | no fallback to stale positive authority; additional capacity scale-triggered | HELD |
| Object safety, quarantine and independent recovery | mandatory for enabled private objects and retained bytes/manifests/lineage/classification | optional media conveniences or deferred object features require disabled scope; existing custody/retention never disappears | HELD |
| Monitoring and observability | mandatory detection, safe-stop visibility and sufficient protected diagnostics/resolver support | extra convenience dashboards optional only with proven baseline coverage; retention/capacity expansion scale-triggered | HELD |
| Environments, deployment, secrets and compatibility | mandatory isolation, provenance, controlled transitions, retirement proof and recovery for enabled scope | unenabled feature environments deferrable only without losing current recovery; extra parallel capacity scale-triggered | HELD |
| Accounts, DNS and provider support | mandatory actual routing, independent recovery access, billing/outage support and named technical actor | redundant convenience channels optional only after baseline independence and support proof; extra routing capacity scale-triggered | HELD |
| Notifications and external effects | mandatory idempotency, intent, reconciliation and failure handling whenever those effects are enabled | convenience notification channels deferrable/optional if no required safety/support outcome depends on them; retained intents still handled | HELD |
| Incident usage, response and reconciliation | mandatory bounded safe stop, protected retained work/data and technical recovery/support duties | no assumed free incident; extra proven burst capacity scale-triggered without bypassing cost stops | HELD |
| Restore and clean-room exit drills | mandatory cross-plane DB/object/audit/floor manifests, isolated verification, overlap, support and cleanup | additional nonrequired convenience exercises optional only after required drill coverage; no deferral of required recovery assurance | HELD |
| External people and technical handoff | mandatory named operation/support/custody/recovery availability and account/legal duties where applicable | extra convenience support optional only if baseline is proven; owner debugging is never a free staffing substitute | HELD |
| AI operations and independent review | mandatory bounded scope/credentials, dry runs, evidence, independent reviews and hard stops for enabled AI work | optional product AI features deferrable while disabled; required task review remains mandatory regardless of model cost | HELD |

The table distinguishes baseline obligations from conditional extra components. It does not declare every potential service purchased or needed in every scenario. An exclusion needs a measured capability/dependency map and evidence that retained work and mandatory assurance remain safe. Ordinary project copies are not independent audit/floor/object custody. DB backup does not cover all recovery planes. Owner labor, incident support and exit overlap cannot be priced implicitly at zero.

## Cost stop and drain-versus-hold reference edges

T-E3-031 owns detailed owner-readable hold behavior and limits. T-E3-019/020/020b/021/022 own queue contract, family coverage/gates, poison/backpressure/cancel/drain and backlog/resolver; T-E3-032/033 and E6 release gates own environment/promotion control. These are task/gate references, not new runtime dependencies or implemented transitions. Queue prerequisites T-E3-001-R1/T-E3-003/T-E3-004 are not proved complete by this document.

Before later acceptance of work, the cost decision must bind the capability's safely funded execution, retained-state protection, reconciliation and stop/drain duties, using an independently verified authorized envelope. Unknown mandatory cost, billing/account outage or missing current evidence holds new affected positive effects; it never permits weaker audit, floors, custody, independence or authorization.

Accepted/in-flight work is not erased by a billing stop. Re-read current authority, floors, audit and runtime compatibility; fence new intake and old consumers. Controlled drain may finish only already accepted work whose current authorization and safe funded envelope are proved. Otherwise stop affected positive effects, preserve stable operation/effect identities, checkpoints, intents and backlog, and reconcile uncertain outcomes as OUTCOME_UNKNOWN/PARTIAL/RECONCILING. Unknown remaining cost is not permission for an unlimited drain. Queue emptiness, worker success or HTTP success is not effect or budget proof. Lease loss cannot cause blind replay. Cancel/stop cannot undo external effects or restore old negatives.

The technical resolver and applicable E6 gate decide controlled execution through their existing authority; the owner gets affected feature, stopped/retained work, risk/cost/recovery and approve/hold/stop/support choices in plain language. The owner is not assigned SQL/SSH, invoices-as-debugging, secret administration or worker recovery. This skeleton implements no meter, watcher, alert, budget action, runtime drain or task scheduler. T-E3-038 invoice/budget watch is separate and remains unperformed.

## Later closure and rejection checks

Before an actual paid/activation decision: fill all scenario/family financial and applicability fields with current evidence; verify safe baseline plus incident/drill/exit/support allocation; name external technical actors and custody; close exact independent review findings and record applicable owner authorization/release gates. Missing/stale/contradictory evidence or an unaffordable mandatory baseline holds the affected capability. A candidate change still needs equal-evidence ADR-006 transition gates; a cheap headline never crowns another runtime.

Reject numeric thresholds invented in this skeleton, unknown-as-zero totals, unchecked optional/deferrable safeguards, synchronous long jobs as a savings plan, unbounded drain, loss of accepted work, assumed owner debugging, untested provider selections or a document/green-CI claim of financial readiness. Task acceptance covers classified slots and the explicit drain-versus-hold references only.

Pack: `[[vault/PACKS/P-E3-030.md]]`; task: `[[vault/REGISTRY/T-E3-030.md]]`; evidence: `[[vault/EVIDENCE/E-DEV-023.md]]`.
